0..85 Comment "/// A definition\'s composite meets `Path.step` over the same paths, at endpoints that"
86..109 Comment "/// stuck calls return."
110..113 Comment "///"
114..200 Comment "/// `concat`\'s body is `Path.step(p, q)`, so a type written with `concat` reads as one"
201..283 Comment "/// written with `Path.step`. At variable endpoints the two read alike. At a stuck"
284..361 Comment "/// call, `concat`\'s type reads the endpoint through the environment its call"
362..448 Comment "/// bound, which holds it. The type written with `Path.step` writes the call in place."
449..452 Comment "///"
453..531 Comment "/// The machine runs the written call where its type reads it. It compares the"
532..611 Comment "/// result with the held endpoint, and the kernel replays the comparison by its"
612..628 Comment "/// own reading."
629..632 Comment "///"
633..706 Comment "/// - see: #4038 — the checker refused the composite at stuck endpoints"
707..793 Comment "/// - see: #4005 — two endpoints a call returned apart, which the code walk hands on"
794..854 Comment "/// - see: #4011 — a bind over a transport stuck on a path"
856..902 Comment "/// The composite of two paths, by definition."
